you  [Music]  your wake up in the morning with a smile  on your face because you already know  it's going to be a good day the sun is  shining and it's really nice breeze on  your skin and you have the whole day  ahead of you and you can pretty much do  whatever you want but the first thing  you do is you gotta water your plan  that's how you feel when you wake up in  stardew valley you have a lot of stuff  to get done there's so much you haven't  accomplished you got this small farm and  it needs a lot of love there's rocks at  trees and grass over growing the whole  area you got to clean it all up there's  a cave with slimes and bats  you got to mine it to the bottom and get  all those minerals there's ponds and  streams an entire ocean to fish there's  a town of people that don't know you  very well and because they don't know  you they don't like you so you got to  make this effort to get to know them I  mean they really don't like you I went  to this dance and no one would dance  with me no one not even you come on I  mean it can kind of feel overwhelming  but if you take it day-by-day and you  just focus on one task at a time it's  pretty amazing how much you can  accomplish start out with a pretty  simple watering can and it takes some  time to water all your crops but once  you get into the swing of things you can  get all your farming work done by about  10:00 a.m. that gives you the rest of  the day to explore the town and do  whatever  there are a lot of options in stardew  valley you can take on tasks from people  in the town there's a town store you can  go to to get new seeds and try out  different types of farming people will  ask for things like fish or a type of  fruit or vegetable you got to collect it  a certain amount of time and deliver it  you can investigate the forest and  forage for items you spend a lot of your  time just walking exploring land  figuring out what you want to do I spent  most of my time in the caves at first  it's pretty rough there's a lot of  little things in the mines that can come  after you and using the pickaxe on the  rocks takes a lot of your energy but if  you can make it down five levels it  opens up an elevator that way the next  time you visit the mines you can take an  elevator to a lower floor as long as you  go down five levels you're slowly  getting better further and further down  the mine you get better loot and you  start getting equipment like boots and  swords and the further you go you can  find really high-end stuff like diamonds  and items that you don't even know what  they are you could take them to a  blacksmith to get them opened up or to a  museum so you can learn more about them  every day I was in the mines I was  progressing but you progressed in every  way and start you tally even when you're  focusing on one thing like getting to  the bottom of that mine as you sell your  harvests and the things that you find  you make enough money to buy things like  a little barn and get some chickens and  then you get to pet them and you get  their eggs a little bit more time and  you get to buy a bigger barn and then  you get some cows and then goats and  maybe a sheep you can turn the milk into  cheese and the eggs into mayonnaise and  the sheep's wool into cloth you can  harvest the crops into jelly and pickles  and oil and beer you get a big farm with  sprinklers that water your crops for you  so you can spend even more time doing  whatever it is that you want to do you  build a life for yourself  and that's my favorite part about  stardew valley there's really no wrong  way to spend your time whether you make  a massive garden or pursue the talents  people or chip away at the mines  wherever you spend your time is good  because you're always progressing no  matter how many days I spent in those  mines I was always taking care of my  farm in the morning I increased my  skills and my items and I kept moving  it's been over a year in the game since  I started I have a big farm a nice house  and a kitchen and I finally made it to  the bottom of that mine now that spring  dance is coming around again and I'm  thinking I might be interested in trying  to get someone to dance with me and  that's what makes stardew valley so  sweet you'll feel rewarded every day for  living the way you want to live so you  can clear out the pathway to investigate  more of the woods or explore the weird  sewer tunnel find out what makes the  howling noises when it rains play an  arcade game at the bar or go on a date  it's up to you day is yours to do with  whatever you want so spend it the way  you want to do it as Joe Dirt would say  life's a garden dig it  [Music]  you  [Music]

